#################################################################
# Ontology node
#################################################################

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/slice-quality-rubric>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> ;
    rdfs:comment """The slice-quality rubric module — the ontology-resident, data-driven rubric the gmeow-dev slice-quality advisor binds to. Quality axes, the lattice tier ladder, per-tier score thresholds, advice text, read-scope coeffects, and dated exemptions are all individuals here; Rust ships only a closed set of measurement primitives the axis descriptors name (the Profile rubric-as-data pattern). Grades form a bounded lattice grounded in logic:QualityValue: the roll-up tier is the UNWEIGHTED meet of the per-axis grades, the ratchet is the lattice order, and the scalar tier is a lossy projection of the full per-axis grade vector.

This slice is its own self-application capstone: it must itself score Maximal on the rubric it defines, and its rationales name no test artifact — it is the exemplar of the provenance-honesty rule it introduces."""@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/slice-quality-rubric> ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Slice-Quality Rubric Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The GMEOW Slice-Quality Rubric Module — classes, properties, and individuals of the GMEOW super-vocabulary that make per-slice quality a queryable, reasoned, data-driven rubric."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxConfigBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox .
